  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/9e00f5aa5603ed937e3a0f3ee607306aeb24a524830a07db6f3d4cdb4bb17683.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$",
